# The corpus is FETCHED, not vendored: tools/conformance/upstream.pin.xon names
# a commit and a digest, and `make fetch` is what turns that into files.  Six
# hundred MIT-licensed .py files do not belong in an MIT-0 bundle, and a copy
# would rot silently where a pin cannot.
deps/

# GENERATED, and both for the same reason: they are facts of this machine, not
# of this bundle.  harness.gen.x embeds two absolute paths; tests/conformance/
# embeds the output of whichever CPython happened to be the oracle.
tests/lib/
tests/conformance/
# The engine link is a MACHINE FACT: tests/spec-runner.sh points it at the
# engine it is already using, so the platform's boot finds the C headers and
# compiles its reader analysers (23.6s -> 7.8s per spec file, measured).
/engine
